# IMPL-PERM_CATALOG essence pseudocode

<!-- [IMPL-PERM_CATALOG] [ARCH-MACOS_PERM_REPORT] [REQ-MACOS_PERM_REPORT] — maps CLI permission aliases to TCC services and database routing -->

## RESOLVE_ALIASES

<!-- [IMPL-PERM_CATALOG] [ARCH-MACOS_PERM_REPORT] [REQ-MACOS_PERM_REPORT] — resolves sponsor-facing aliases to canonical PermissionEntry records -->

```
INPUT: optional alias list from CLI (--permission flags)
OUTPUT: PermissionEntry[] — full catalog or filtered subset
PRE: each alias when provided must exist in PERMISSION_CATALOG
POST: unknown alias raises CatalogError with alias name
EFFECTS: none (pure lookup)
```

```
DATA PERMISSION_CATALOG = [
  { alias: "screen", service: "kTCCServiceScreenCapture", label: "Screen Recording", database: "system" },
  { alias: "microphone", service: "kTCCServiceMicrophone", label: "Microphone", database: "user" },
  { alias: "camera", service: "kTCCServiceCamera", label: "Camera", database: "user" },
  { alias: "accessibility", service: "kTCCServiceAccessibility", label: "Accessibility", database: "system" },
  { alias: "input-monitoring", service: "kTCCServiceListenEvent", label: "Input Monitoring", database: "system" },
  { alias: "input-injection", service: "kTCCServicePostEvent", label: "Input Injection", database: "system" },
  { alias: "full-disk-access", service: "kTCCServiceSystemPolicyAllFiles", label: "Full Disk Access", database: "system" },
  { alias: "developer-tools", service: "kTCCServiceDeveloperTool", label: "Developer Tools", database: "system" }
]

IF aliases is empty THEN
  RETURN PERMISSION_CATALOG
ELSE
  FOR EACH alias IN aliases
    IF alias NOT IN PERMISSION_CATALOG THEN RAISE CatalogError(alias)
  RETURN filtered entries
```

## ROUTE_TO_DATABASE

<!-- same token set — groups PermissionEntry by database source for reader -->

```
INPUT: PermissionEntry[]
OUTPUT: { user: PermissionEntry[], system: PermissionEntry[] }
POST: every entry appears in exactly one bucket by entry.database
```
